// Function Node: Build Worker Task List

const taskDivision = $json.body.taskDivision;
const workers = $json.body.workers;

// Create array of workers with their assigned tasks and ports
const workerTaskList = workers.map((worker) => {
  return {
    workerName: worker.workerName,
    port: worker.port,
    task: taskDivision['tasks'][worker.workerName],
    status: worker.status,
    pid: worker.pid
  };
});

return workerTaskList;

tasks.Soldier1:
COMBAT MISSION: Make Soldier1 and Soldier2 spar in a non-lethal internal PvP duel, stopping when either reaches 6 hearts health or when time expires.

Location: Near near shared rally point / current position
Role: Soldier1
Combat Role: DUELIST

OBJECTIVE: Fight Soldier2 in a controlled, non-lethal sparring match, practicing melee combat while avoiding killing blows.

POSITION: You start 5 blocks east of the target at coordinates (232, -60, -467).



TARGET: undefined

EQUIPMENT: Weapon: best available melee (sword/axe/fists), Armor: whatever equipped

TACTICS:
1. Use COMPLETE COMBAT TEMPLATE as structural base.
2. Set SOLDIER_NAME = 'Soldier1'.
3. TARGET_TYPE is a player/bot named 'Soldier2' (friendly bot PvP).
4. Use PvP target acquisition instead of mob search:
let target = bot.players['Soldier2']?.entity;
if (!target || target.position.distanceTo(bot.entity.position) > 30) {
  target = null;
}
5. Set RETREAT_HEALTH = 14 (7 hearts) per PvP rules, but ALSO enforce non-lethal spar stop at 6 hearts (12 HP).
6. Non-lethal spar logic (inside loop): if bot.health <= 12 OR (target && target.health !== undefined && target.health <= 12) then stop attacking, log that sparring limit reached, and break the loop.
7. Weapon handling MUST follow the safe equipment pattern and log status:
const weapon = bot.inventory.items().find(i => i.name.includes('sword')) || 
               bot.inventory.items().find(i => i.name.includes('axe')) || 
               null;
console.log('[Soldier1] Weapon:', weapon ? weapon.name : 'NONE (fists - low damage!)');
if (weapon) await bot.equip(weapon, 'hand');
8. Use COMPLETE COMBAT TEMPLATE loop with these PvP-specific parameters:
- MAX_COMBAT_TIME = 60000 ms (60 seconds).
- SEARCH_RANGE = 30.
- MELEE_RANGE = 3.5.
- RETREAT_HEALTH = 14, but also check stopAtHealth = 12 for sparring non-lethal condition.
- At top of each while iteration, FIRST check timeout, SECOND health/stopAtHealth, then range, then movement/attack.
9. Movement and engagement:
- If distance <= MELEE_RANGE: attack with await bot.attack(target).
- If distance > MELEE_RANGE but <= 30: close distance using bot.setControlState('forward', true) and 'sprint', wait ~300 ms with skills.wait, then stop movement.
- If distance > 30 OR target is missing, break the loop.
10. Maintain duel spacing around 3–6 blocks; avoid running far from rallyPoint. If distance from rallyPoint exceeds ~30 blocks, disengage.
11. No killing blows: rely on stopAtHealth=12 check to break before lethal damage.
12. End conditions: target invalid/out of range, timeout, stopAtHealth reached, or retreatHealth reached; log final health and exit cleanly.

RETREAT CONDITION: bot.health < 14 OR bot.health <= 12 (spar stop) OR target.health <= 12 OR target distance > 30 blocks OR combat time > 60 seconds.

CONSTRAINTS:
- This is INTERNAL_PVP sparring: lethal must be false; stop attacking at or before 6 hearts (12 HP) for either participant.
- MUST use COMPLETE COMBAT TEMPLATE structure with PvP target acquisition and added non-lethal health checks.
- MUST include timeout check with MAX_COMBAT_TIME = 60000 ms at the start of the loop.
- MUST log weapon status and equip the best available melee weapon.
- MUST check MELEE_RANGE = 3.5 before attacking and use movement to close distance.
- Do NOT use bot.pathfinder or any GoalNear/GoalBlock/GoalFollow/GoalXZ or bot.navigate.
- Do NOT use skills.stay(bot, -1).
- Do NOT use infinite loops such as while (true).

BANNED CODE (DO NOT USE - WILL BREAK):
BANNED: bot.pathfinder
BANNED: GoalNear
BANNED: GoalBlock
BANNED: GoalFollow
BANNED: bot.navigate

REQUIRED CODE PATTERNS:
USE: Object.values(bot.entities).find()
USE: bot.lookAt(target.position)
USE: bot.attack(target)
USE: skills.wait(bot, 300)

ATTACK CODE TEMPLATE (ACTIVE DEBUG VERSION):
console.log('[Soldier1] === COMBAT START ===');
console.log('[Soldier1] Position:', bot.entity.position);

const weapon = bot.inventory.items().find(i => i.name.includes('sword')) || bot.inventory.items().find(i => i.name.includes('axe')) || null;
console.log('[Soldier1] Weapon:', weapon ? weapon.name : 'NONE (fists)');
if (weapon) await bot.equip(weapon, 'hand');

const allEntities = Object.values(bot.entities).filter(e => e.name);
console.log('[Soldier1] All entities I see:', allEntities.slice(0, 10).map(e => e.name + '(' + Math.floor(e.position.distanceTo(bot.entity.position)) + 'm)').join(', '));

let target = Object.values(bot.entities).find(e => e.name && e.name.toLowerCase().includes('hostile mob') && e.position.distanceTo(bot.entity.position) < 50);
console.log('[Soldier1] Target hostile mob:', target ? 'FOUND at ' + Math.floor(target.position.distanceTo(bot.entity.position)) + ' blocks' : 'NOT FOUND');

if (target) {
  console.log('[Soldier1] Starting attack loop');
  let hits = 0;
  while (target && target.isValid) {
    if (bot.health < 12) {
      console.log('[Soldier1] Low health, retreating');
      await skills.moveAway(bot, 10);
      break;
    }
    await bot.lookAt(target.position);
    await bot.attack(target);
    hits++;
    if (hits % 3 === 0) console.log('[Soldier1] Hits: ' + hits);
    await skills.wait(bot, 300);
    target = bot.entities[target.id];
  }
  console.log('[Soldier1] Combat done, total hits: ' + hits);
} else {
  console.log('[Soldier1] ERROR: No hostile mob found within 50 blocks!');
}

console.log('[Soldier1] Holding position');



COMBAT ZONE:
- Your Start Position: (232, -60, -467)
- Rally Point: (227, -60, -467)
- Max Chase Distance: 20 blocks from rally point
- Your Approach: east side

TEAMMATES: Soldier2
- Keep 3+ blocks from teammates
- Stay on YOUR side of target

REMINDERS:
- You are ALREADY positioned - do NOT use pathfinder
- bot.attack() automatically walks into melee range
- If you write pathfinder anywhere the code will BREAK
- Use the EXACT code template above including all console.log lines

